## Final test\n\n**Did this create shipped value, decision value, or reusable machinery?** If not — keep working or state the real blocker.\n","stdout":"═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n⛔ SPECTRASYNQ AGENT EXECUTION STANDARD — LOAD-BEARING ⛔\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\nBrief = FLOOR not ceiling. Faithful reproduction of bad work = FAILURE.\nThree bars (ALL required): FIDELITY + CRAFT + VALUE.\nProof on stop. No report theatre. No obedient dogshit.\nCANON: docs/agent/AGENT_EXECUTION_STANDARD.md\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n# ⛔ AGENT EXECUTION STANDARD — LOAD-BEARING\n\n**Full canon:** `docs/agent/AGENT_EXECUTION_STANDARD.md` — read it on first session in this repo.\n\n## Prime law\n\nThe brief is the **floor**, not the ceiling. Faithful reproduction of bad work is **failure**. Gates are survival checks, not ambition.\n\n## Three bars (all required)\n\n1. **Fidelity** — constraints, provenance, Captain decisions, repo boundaries, safety.\n2. **Craft** — fix weak composition, hierarchy, motion, workflows, unclear outputs.\n3. **Value** — shipped value, decision value, or reusable machinery.\n\nPassing only fidelity is **bureaucratic failure**.\n\n## Operating rules (non-negotiable)\n\n- Weak prototype ≠ sacred. Do not preserve weakness unless ordered.\n- Mediocre path → surface conflict **before** editing files.\n- Agent-resolvable blockers → resolve. Captain gets **decisions**, not chores.\n- No report theatre. No doctrine cathedrals. No symbolic busy work.\n- No completion without proof. \"I followed the brief\" is not a defence.\n\n## Proof on stop\n\nReturn: **files changed · commands run · validation · screenshots/renders/logs · blockers · next step**.\n\n## Visual / render (SpectraSynq)\n\nComparison is the battlefield. Alpha proof for transparency. No opaque-black-baked reuse. Alpha-bounds before layout compare. Stamp provisional geometry.\n\n## Final tes