{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cd4UDk13oaoZjVBgo51Hw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RzydP1YnwyNRMpbRjFdUMr","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"K1EV format research (read-only)","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"k1ev-format-researcher","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are executing Ruflo task-1784147109798-2h88wn (agent id k1ev-format-researcher) in a hierarchical Ruflo swarm (swarm-1784147099433-oai2dm) for the K1 firmware repo at /private/tmp/k1-ruflo-live.\n\nREAD-ONLY task. Do not edit any files. Do not touch firmware, hardware, or run pio/upload commands.\n\nRead these two files in full:\n- SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1ev_capture.h\n- SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1_ap_capture_telemetry.cpp (focus on k1ev_capture_dump call site and the k1ev_dump serial command dispatch near the bottom)\n- SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1ev_capture.cpp (the actual dump formatter, function k1ev_capture_dump)\n\nProduce a precise, complete specification of the CURRENT frozen `[K1EV]` buffered wire format as actually emitted by k1ev_capture_dump() in k1ev_capture.cpp (this is the ACTUAL implementation, not the header comment — verify byte-for-byte against the real snprintf format strings). Cover:\n\n1. Wrapper lines: `K1EV_CAPTURE_BEGIN,count=<N>,capacity=<N>,dropped=<N>` (printed once, at start) and `K1EV_CAPTURE_DONE,count=<N>,dropped=<N>` (once, at end). Exact field order and types (uint32).\n2. Per-sample line format: `[K1EV] t_ms=%lu event_ms=%lu ev=%lu onset=%d bass=%d kick=%d snare=%d hihat=%d kid=%lu sid=%lu hid=%lu beat=%d bphase=%.3f bconf=%.3f bpm=%.1f` — exact field names, order, printf types.\n3. The optional has_chroma suffix appended ONLY when flags bit 0x40 is set: ` croot=%d ctype=%d cconf=%.3f chroma=<v0>;<v1>;...;<v11>` (12 semicolon-joined %.3f chroma values, croot is A-origin int, -1 sentinel when ctype==0/NONE) followed by ` mode=%u photons=%.3f`.\n4. Value ranges/semantics: bphase/bconf are 0..1 scaled *1000 back to float (3dp); bpm scaled *10 (1dp); chroma/cconf scaled *1000 (3dp); croot range -1..11; ctype range 0..4 (0=NONE,1=MAJOR,2=MINOR,3=DIMINISHED,4=AUGMENTED); mode is uint8 applied_mode; photons is raw unbounded float (%f default precision, no explicit width — check the actual printf spec used, note it's just %.3f per the code).\n5. Line termination: '\\n' appended manually via snprintf then buffer write (not USBSerial.println) — confirm this from the code.\n6. Any onset-frame vs sample-frame distinction that affects which fields are present (onset-only frames omit the chroma suffix entirely).\n\nReturn your findings as clear structured text (not a file) — a future agent will use it directly to write a parser without re-reading the source. Be exact about printf format specifiers so the parser regex/parsing logic matches losslessly (e.g. is bpm always exactly 1 decimal digit, is photons precision fixed at 3 decimals or default C printf %.3f -- check the actual code, not the header comment, since header comments can drift).\n\nWhen done, call mcp__ruflo__task_complete with taskId \"task-1784147109798-2h88wn\" and a result object summarizing the format. Then call mcp__ruflo__hooks_task-completed with taskId \"task-1784147109798-2h88wn\", success true."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1659,"cache_read_input_tokens":179919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1659},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16a76e6c-f56d-436e-9309-aa9c7ce3989f","uuid":"e236d607-ac52-46ec-ae4b-23859af49537","request_id":"req_011Cd4UDiSJDMjQcbhHfF4Dr"}
