{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RvmK2zqJqHDnQ78N8tTa7v","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#pragma once\n2\t// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3\t// Mode-A `[K1EV]` BUFFERED telemetry capture  (K1 Offline Analysis Pairing).\n4\t// Contract: k1-analysis-harness/capture/CAPTURE_CONTRACT.md v0.2.\n5\t//\n6\t// Supersedes the live per-frame emit in serial/k1ev_stream.h. That tap formatted\n7\t// and wrote ~200 chars over USBSerial EVERY audio frame from the loop() post-tempo\n8\t// call site, which perturbed the very pipeline it measures (measured active_p95\n9\t// 8448 us against a 7500 us budget; the shipping DSP already sits ~7040 us p95).\n10\t//\n11\t// This unit instead APPENDS a compact fixed-point struct per frame (sub-us, no\n12\t// printf, no USB) into a PSRAM ring, then formats + emits the WHOLE run AFTER it,\n13\t// off the hot path — exactly like ap_nov_capture / ap_cad_capture. The dump\n14\t// reproduces the FROZEN `[K1EV]` wire format byte-for-byte (see k1ev_capture.cpp),\n15\t// so capture/parse_capture.py is unchanged.\n16\t//\n17\t// ADDITIVE + gated: nothing here compiles unless ENABLE_K1EV_STREAM is defined\n18\t// (only [env:k1_bench_ap_frontend_probe]); k1_prod_im73d / k1_hardware stay\n19\t// byte-identical.\n20\t//\n21\t// Field notes (see CAPTURE_CONTRACT.md §v0.2 / k1ev_stream.h history):\n22\t//  * t_ms   = snap.frame_ms  — FRESH every frame (NOT event.event_ms, stale between\n23\t//             onsets; carried separately as event_ms).\n24\t//  * beat=  = tempo beat_tick (k1_tempo_read), NOT the onset event's beat flag.\n25\t//  * croot / chroma are A-ORIGIN (bin 0 = A); the harness rotates +9 to C-origin.\n26\t//  * croot  = -1 synthesised when chord.type == NONE (0 would collide with A).\n27\t//  * ctype  enum: 0=NONE,1=MAJOR,2=MINOR,3=DIMINISHED,4=AUGMENTED.\n28\t// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n29\t#ifdef ENABLE_K1EV_STREAM\n30\t#include <stdint.h>\n31\t#include \"k1_audio_snapshot.h\"   // K1AudioSnapshot, K1OnsetBeatEvent, K1ChordType, K1_CHROMA_PC_BINS\n32\t\n33\t#ifndef K1EV_STREAM_DECIMATE\n34\t#define K1EV_STREAM_DECIMATE 3   // heavy (chroma) sample cadence: every Nth in-window\n35\t#endif                           // frame. 3 -> 44.4 Hz at the 133 Hz AP rate. Onset\n36\t                                 // frames ALWAYS append (chroma optional to the parser).\n37\t#ifndef K1EV_CAPTURE_CAPACITY\n38\t#define K1EV_CAPTURE_CAPACITY 65536   // 65536 * 64 B = 4 MiB PSRAM (of 8 MiB N16R8). Sized for\n39\t#endif                                // the longest corpus track (Sgadi Li Mi 300.6 s) at the\n40\t                                      // MEASURED 107 samples/s (48,231 w/ 1.5 safety) AND the\n41\t                                      // absolute every-frame-@133Hz worst case (60,118) -> both\n42\t                                      // < 65,536. 32,768 (2 MiB) overflowed both. Alloc fails\n43\t                                      // safe (arm returns false) if 4 MiB PSRAM is unavailable.\n44\t#ifndef K1EV_CAPTURE_MAX_MS\n45\t#define K1EV_CAPTURE_MAX_MS 180000UL  // mirror AP_NOV_CAPTURE_MAX_MS (the piggyback arm\n46\t#endif                                // duration comes straight from nov_capture=<ms>).\n47\t\n48\t// Compact per-frame record (64 B, naturally aligned; sizeof == 64 — static_assert'd\n49\t// in the .cpp). Floats are scaled to int16 with a saturating helper and re-expanded\n50\t// in the dump to the exact %.3f/%.1f the live emit produced (round(x*S)/S == %.Nf(x)).\n51\t// photons is stored full-precision (float) because the director scalar has no bounded\n52\t// range, so a fixed 16-bit scale would risk overflow / clipping.\n53\tstruct K1EVCaptureSample {\n54\t  uint32_t t_ms;            // snap.frame_ms                (always)\n55\t  uint32_t event_ms;        // ev.event_ms                  (always)\n56\t  uint32_t event_id;        // ev.event_id                  (always)\n57\t  uint32_t kick_event_id;   // ev.kick_event_id             (always)\n58\t  uint32_t snare_event_id;  // ev.snare_event_id            (always)\n59\t  uint32_t hihat_event_id;  // ev.hihat_event_id            (always)\n60\t  float    photons;         // photons_scalar (%.3f)        (sample frame)\n61\t  int16_t  bphase_q;        // phase01           * 1000 (%.3f)  (always)\n62\t  int16_t  bconf_q;         // confidence        * 1000 (%.3f)  (always)\n63\t  int16_t  bpm_q10;         // bpm               * 10   (%.1f)  (always)\n64\t  int16_t  cconf_q;         // chord.confidence  * 1000 (%.3f)  (sample frame)\n65\t  int16_t  chroma_q[12];    // chroma_pc[c]      * 1000 (%.3f)  (sample frame)\n66\t  uint8_t  flags;           // b0 onset|b1 bass|b2 kick|b3 snare|b4 hihat|b5 beat_tick|b6 has_chroma\n67\t  int8_t   croot;           // A-origin root; -1 on NONE        (sample frame)\n68\t  uint8_t  ctype;           // 0=NONE..4=AUG                    (sample frame)\n69\t  uint8_t  mode;            // applied_mode                     (sample frame)\n70\t};\n71\t\n72\t// State (external linkage; defined in k1ev_capture.cpp). Shared between the loop()\n73\t// tick call site (.ino) and the arm/dump piggyback in k1_ap_capture_telemetry.cpp.\n74\textern K1EVCaptureSample* K1EV_CAPTURE_BUFFER;\n75\textern uint32_t K1EV_CAPTURE_COUNT;\n76\textern uint32_t K1EV_CAPTURE_DROPPED;\n77\textern uint32_t K1EV_CAPTURE_FRAME_N;\n78\textern uint32_t K1EV_CAPTURE_START_MS;\n79\textern uint32_t K1EV_CAPTURE_END_MS;\n80\textern bool     K1EV_CAPTURE_ACTIVE;\n81\textern bool     K1EV_CAPTURE_ALLOC_FAILED;\n82\t\n83\tbool k1ev_capture_ensure_buffer();                 // lazy PSRAM alloc (internal fallback)\n84\tbool k1ev_capture_arm(uint32_t duration_ms);       // reset + window; piggybacked by nov arm\n85\tvoid k1ev_capture_tick(const K1AudioSnapshot& snap, const K1OnsetBeatEvent& ev);  // hot path: append only\n86\tvoid k1ev_capture_dump();                          // off hot path; piggybacked by nov dump\n87\t\n88\t#endif  // ENABLE_K1EV_STREAM\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RzydP1YnwyNRMpbRjFdUMr","session_id":"16a76e6c-f56d-436e-9309-aa9c7ce3989f","uuid":"1c09d734-7cfa-4c47-8956-b86786ea2f2d","timestamp":"2026-07-15T20:25:39.708Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"K1EV format research (read-only)"}
