{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cd4UDk13oaoZjVBgo51Hw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019hSTdbYSrDRtayTkVr2QNF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"K1EV test design (read-only)","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"k1ev-test-designer","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are executing Ruflo task-1784147111965-qn9m4i (agent id k1ev-test-designer) in a hierarchical Ruflo swarm (swarm-1784147099433-oai2dm) for the K1 firmware repo at /private/tmp/k1-ruflo-live.\n\nREAD-ONLY task. Do not edit any files. Do not write code yet — this is a test design pass only.\n\nRead these two files in full (read-only):\n- SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1ev_capture.h\n- SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1ev_capture.cpp (the k1ev_capture_dump function is the actual wire format source of truth)\n\nAlso skim tests/ directory structure (just `ls tests/` and look at one or two existing *_replay.py or *_static.py test files, e.g. anything parsing a similar buffered/capture serial format like NOV_CAPTURE or APCAD_CAPTURE) to match this repo's existing pytest conventions (fixture style, assertions, file layout) — do NOT read the whole test suite, just enough to match house style.\n\nDesign a focused, non-redundant test plan (no code, just a clear enumerated test list with intent per test) for a host-side parser/validator of the REAL buffered [K1EV] format:\n\n1. Wrapper parsing: K1EV_CAPTURE_BEGIN,count=N,capacity=N,dropped=N and K1EV_CAPTURE_DONE,count=N,dropped=N — correct extraction, count/dropped consistency check (dropped implies count hit capacity), capacity matches the compiled K1EV_CAPTURE_CAPACITY (65536) if that's asserted anywhere.\n2. Base-only per-sample line (no has_chroma bit): correct field extraction, correct type coercion (ints vs floats), absence of croot/ctype/cconf/chroma/mode/photons in that line.\n3. has_chroma sample line: correct extraction of croot (-1..11), ctype (0..4 enum), cconf, exactly 12 semicolon-separated chroma floats, mode, photons.\n4. croot == -1 sentinel case correlates with ctype == 0 (NONE) — a semantic invariant worth asserting in the validator, not just a parse test.\n5. Malformed/truncated line handling: parser should raise/report a clear error, not silently produce wrong data — decide what \"reject\" means (raise ValueError vs return None) matching repo conventions from the reference test file you skimmed.\n6. Count of parsed sample lines matches the BEGIN/DONE count field (equality invariant) minus expected drops.\n7. Any other edge case you find worth covering given the ACTUAL emit code (e.g. flags bit decoding for onset/bass/kick/snare/hihat/beat as 0/1 ints, event id fields as unsigned, bpm always 1 decimal, bphase/bconf/cconf/chroma always 3 decimals).\n\nReturn the test plan as clear structured text (not a file). Note the repo's pytest file naming convention you observed (test_<module>_<scenario>.py) so the implementer names the new file consistently.\n\nWhen done, call mcp__ruflo__task_complete with taskId \"task-1784147111965-qn9m4i\" and a result object summarizing the test plan. Then call mcp__ruflo__hooks_task-completed with taskId \"task-1784147111965-qn9m4i\", success true."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1659,"cache_read_input_tokens":179919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1659},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16a76e6c-f56d-436e-9309-aa9c7ce3989f","uuid":"a7fcc42c-f510-4566-8e89-bd36a606dddd","request_id":"req_011Cd4UDiSJDMjQcbhHfF4Dr"}
