g *_replay.py or *_static.py test files, e.g. anything parsing a similar buffered/capture serial format like NOV_CAPTURE or APCAD_CAPTURE) to match this repo's existing pytest conventions (fixture style, assertions, file layout) — do NOT read the whole test suite, just enough to match house style.\n\nDesign a focused, non-redundant test plan (no code, just a clear enumerated test list with intent per test) for a host-side parser/validator of the REAL buffered [K1EV] format:\n\n1. Wrapper parsing: K1EV_CAPTURE_BEGIN,count=N,capacity=N,dropped=N and K1EV_CAPTURE_DONE,count=N,dropped=N — correct extraction, count/dropped consistency check (dropped implies count hit capacity), capacity matches the compiled K1EV_CAPTURE_CAPACITY (65536) if that's asserted anywhere.\n2. Base-only per-sample line (no has_chroma bit): correct field extraction, correct type coercion (ints vs floats), absence of croot/ctype/cconf/chroma/mode/photons in that line.\n3. has_chroma sample line: correct extraction of croot (-1..11), ctype (0..4 enum), cconf, exactly 12 semicolon-separated chroma floats, mode, photons.\n4. croot == -1 sentinel case correlates with ctype == 0 (NONE) — a semantic invariant worth asserting in the validator, not just a parse test.\n5. Malformed/truncated line handling: parser should raise/report a clear error, not silently produce wrong data — decide what \"reject\" means (raise ValueError vs return None) matching repo conventions from the reference test file you skimmed.\n6. Count of parsed sample lines matches the BEGIN/DONE count field (equality invariant) minus expected drops.\n7. Any other edge case you find worth covering given the ACTUAL emit code (e.g. flags bit decoding for onset/bass/kick/snare/hihat/beat as 0/1 ints, event id fields as unsigned, bpm always 1 decimal, bphase/bconf/cconf/chroma always 3 decimals).\n\nReturn the test plan as clear structured text (not a file). Note the repo's pytest file naming convention you observed (test_<module>_<scenario>.py) so the implementer names the new file consistently.\n\nWhen done, call mcp__ruflo__task_complete with taskId \"task-1784147111965-qn9m4i\" and a result object summarizing the test plan. Then call mcp__ruflo__hooks_task-completed with taskId \"task-1784147111965-qn9m4i\", success true.\n<context_window_protection>\n  <priority_instructions>\n    Raw tool output floods context window. MUST use context-mode MCP tools. Keep raw data in sandbox.\n  </priority_instructions>\n\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \"timeline\")\n       - After resume, check prior context before asking user.\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands, auto-indexes, searches. ONE call replaces many steps.\n       - Each command: {label: \"section header\", command: \"shell command\"}\n       - label becomes FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\"q1\", \"q2\", ...])\n       - All follow-up questions. ONE call, many queries (default relevance mode).\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\n       - API calls, log analysis, data processing.\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\n\n  <forbidden_actions>\n    - NO Bash for commands producing >20 lines output.\n    - NO Read for analysis — use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read IS correct for files you intend to Edit.\n    - NO WebFetch — use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index.\n    - Bash ONLY for git/mkdir/rm/mv/navigation.\n    - NO mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file creation/modification.\n      mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute is for analysis, processing, computation only.\n  </forbidden_actions>\n\n  <file_writing_policy>\n    ALWAYS use native Write/Edit tools for file creation/modification.\n    NEVER use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, or Bash to write files.\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\n  </file_writing_policy>\n\n  <output_constraints>\n    <artifact_policy>\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to FILES. NEVER inline.\n      Return only: file path + 1-line description.\n    </artifact_policy>\n  </output_constraints>\n  <session_continuity>\n    Skills, roles, and decisions set during this session remain active until the user revokes them.\n    Do not drop behavioral directives as context grows.\n  </session_continuity>\n\n</context_window_protection>","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-private-tmp-k1-ruflo-live/16a76e6c-f56d-436e-9309-aa9c7ce3989f/tasks/a301bc0ca6189cd83.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
