{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cd4UFwXu2qo5GmdyGBiLA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Have all needed evidence. Reporting findings and completing the task.\n\n## `[K1EV]` buffered wire format — verified against source (2026-07-16)\n\nSource of truth: `SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1ev_capture.cpp` (`k1ev_capture_dump`, lines 158-207), struct/gate in `k1ev_capture.h`, dispatch in `k1_ap_capture_telemetry.cpp` lines 885-894.\n\n**Gate:** entire TU compiles only under `ENABLE_K1EV_STREAM` (set only in `env:k1_bench_ap_frontend_probe`). Dispatch command is `k1ev_dump=1`, decoupled — sent AFTER the `nov_dump`/`nov` flow completes, so it does not interfere with `device_novelty_buffer_capture.py`'s `read_until_done()` marker scan.\n\n### 1. Wrapper lines\nEmitted via `USBSerial.print`/`println` (NOT the per-sample snprintf path), each exactly once:\n\n- Start (before any sample lines):\n  `K1EV_CAPTURE_BEGIN,count=<uint32>,capacity=<uint32>,dropped=<uint32>`\n  Field order: count, capacity, dropped. All printed via `USBSerial.print(uint32_t)` (Arduino's native unsigned-int-to-decimal conversion — no leading zeros, no explicit width).\n- End (after all sample lines):\n  `K1EV_CAPTURE_DONE,count=<uint32>,dropped=<uint32>`\n  Only two fields here (no capacity). Terminated with `println` (`\\n`, and on Arduino frameworks that means exactly `\\n`, not `\\r\\n`, since `USBSerial.println` on ESP32 Arduino core appends `\"\\r\\n\"` actually — **verify**: Arduino `Print::println` always appends `\"\\r\\n\"`. The BEGIN/DONE lines use `println`, so they end `\\r\\n`. The per-sample lines use manual `b[p++]='\\n'` — only `\\n`, no `\\r`.** This is an important asymmetry for a parser.**\n\n### 2. Per-sample line format\nBuilt via `snprintf` into a 384-byte stack buffer `b`, one call per sample, written with `USBSerial.write((const uint8_t*)b, p)` — i.e. **not `println`**, so per-sample lines are plain `\\n`-terminated only (added manually at line 194-196, only if `p < sizeof(b)-1`).\n\nFixed prefix (always present, exact literal from the code):\n```\n[K1EV] t_ms=%lu event_ms=%lu ev=%lu onset=%d bass=%d kick=%d snare=%d hihat=%d kid=%lu sid=%lu hid=%lu beat=%d bphase=%.3f bconf=%.3f bpm=%.1f\n```\nArgs in order, exact C types passed:\n- `t_ms` = `(unsigned long)s.t_ms` — %lu\n- `event_ms` = `(unsigned long)s.event_ms` — %lu\n- `ev` = `(unsigned long)s.event_id` — %lu\n- `onset`,`bass`,`kick`,`snare`,`hihat` = `int` 0/1 (from flag bits 0x01/0x02/0x04/0x08/0x10) — %d\n- `kid` = `(unsigned long)s.kick_event_id` — %lu\n- `sid` = `(unsigned long)s.snare_event_id` — %lu\n- `hid` = `(unsigned long)s.hihat_event_id` — %lu\n- `beat` = `int` 0/1 from flag bit 0x20 (this is `tev.beat_tick`, the tempo-flywheel beat tick, **NOT** `ev.beat` from the onset event — confirmed by comment at capture.cpp:134)\n- `bphase` = `(double)s.bphase_q / 1000.0` printed `%.3f` — always exactly 3 decimal digits (fixed by format spec, not \"default precision\")\n- `bconf` = `(double)s.bconf_q / 1000.0` printed `%.3f` — always 3 decimals\n- `bpm` = `(double)s.bpm_q10 / 10.0` printed `%.1f` — always exactly 1 decimal digit\n\nAll of these (\"always present prefix fields\") are written by `k1ev_capture_tick` unconditionally for every appended sample (onset-frame or sample-frame).\n\n### 3. Optional chroma/chord/mode/photons suffix — gated on flags bit `0x40` (has_chroma)\nBit 0x40 is set ONLY when `sample_frame` is true (i.e. `frame_n % K1EV_STREAM_DECIMATE == 0`, decimate=3 → ~44.4Hz at 133Hz AP rate). It is **not** set on onset-only frames that aren't also a decimated sample frame — confirmed by capture.cpp:136-150 comment: \"On onset-only frames the heavy fields are intentionally left unwritten... the dump reads them ONLY when the has_chroma bit is set.\"\n\nWhen `s.flags & 0x40`:\n```\n croot=%d ctype=%d cconf=%.3f chroma=\n```\n(leading space before `croot`, appended directly onto the prefix line — no newline before it)\n- `croot` = `(int)s.croot` — %d. Range: **-1..11** (A-origin pitch-class index 0=A..11; -1 sentinel synthesized when `chord.type==NONE`, per k1ev_capture.h comment and capture.cpp:139 `have_chord ? rootNote : -1`).\n- `ctype` = `(int)s.ctype` — %d. Range **0..4**: 0=NONE, 1=MAJOR, 2=MINOR, 3=DIMINISHED, 4=AUGMENTED (matches `K1ChordType` enum order, per header comment line 27).\n- `cconf` = `(double)s.cconf_q / 1000.0` — %.3f, always 3 decimals.\n- Then `chroma=` immediately followed by 12 semicolon-joined `%.3f` values, no space around `;`, format loop: first value plain `\"%.3f\"`, subsequent values `\";%.3f\"` (line 189-191). Exactly `K1_CHROMA_PC_BINS` = 12 values (static_assert'd at capture.cpp:29). Values = `s.chroma_q[c] / 1000.0`, each 3 decimals.\n- Loop has a truncation guard `p < (int)sizeof(b) - 12` — with buf size 384 this is not expected to trigger in practice but a parser should not assume the chroma list is always exactly 12 entries if buffer truncation were ever hit (it won't be under normal line lengths, but note it's not a hard guarantee at the format-string level, only an empirical one).\n- After the chroma list: ` mode=%u photons=%.3f`\n  - `mode` = `(unsigned)s.mode` — %u, uint8 `applied_mode` (small int, printed as unsigned decimal, no leading zeros/width).\n  - `photons` = `(double)s.photons` — **%.3f**, i.e. exactly 3 decimal digits fixed by the format spec (not printf's unspecified default 6-digit precision — the code explicitly writes `%.3f`, so precision is pinned at 3). `photons` itself is stored full-precision `float` (unbounded/unscaled, unlike the other quantised int16 fields), so its printed value can be any magnitude but always rendered to 3 decimal places.\n\n### 4. Line termination summary\n- BEGIN/DONE wrapper lines: `USBSerial.println(...)` → terminated `\\r\\n` (Arduino `Print::println` semantics).\n- Per-sample `[K1EV] ...` lines: built with `snprintf` into `b`, manually terminated with a single `'\\n'` byte appended at buffer position `p` (only if room remains), then written raw via `USBSerial.write()` — **`\\n` only, no `\\r`**. A parser must handle both terminator styles or simply split on `\\n` and strip trailing `\\r` if present (safe for both cases).\n\n### 5. Onset-frame vs sample-frame distinction (governs field presence)\n- `onset_frame` = `ev.onset || ev.bass_onset || ev.kick || ev.snare || ev.hihat || ev.beat` (note: uses `ev.beat`, the onset-event's own beat flag, purely to decide whether to *append* a sample — NOT the printed `beat=` field, which comes from `tev.beat_tick`).\n- `sample_frame` = every Nth frame per `K1EV_STREAM_DECIMATE` (=3), counted via `K1EV_CAPTURE_FRAME_N++` on every tick call regardless of onset status.\n- A sample is appended (row exists) if `onset_frame || sample_frame`.\n- The chroma/chord/mode/photons suffix appears **only if that particular appended row happened to also be a `sample_frame`** (bit 0x40). An onset-only row that is not also a decimated sample_frame will have the prefix line with NO suffix at all — this is the \"onset-only frames omit the chroma suffix entirely\" case, confirmed exactly by the code and its comment.\n- Consequently a parser must branch line handling strictly on presence/absence of ` croot=` in the line (or equivalently check for the space-prefixed `croot=` substring after the fixed prefix), not assume it based on `onset=`/`beat=` field values — a frame can be both onset AND a decimated sample_frame (has both onset flags set true and the chroma suffix present).\n\n### Buffer/capacity context (not wire-format but relevant to `count`/`capacity`/`dropped`)\n`K1EV_CAPTURE_CAPACITY` = 65536 (4 MiB PSRAM, `k1ev_capture.h` line 38, changed from 32768 per repo history/commit `67594ba`). `K1EV_CAPTURE_MAX_MS` = 180000 (mirrors `AP_NOV_CAPTURE_MAX_MS`). Each buffered record `K1EVCaptureSample` is exactly 64 bytes (static_assert'd).\n\nFiles read (read-only, no edits made): `SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1ev_capture.h`, `SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1ev_capture.cpp`, `SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/serial/k1_ap_capture_telemetry.cpp` (dispatch site lines 885-894).\n\nNow completing the Ruflo task."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":126374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":878,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RzydP1YnwyNRMpbRjFdUMr","session_id":"16a76e6c-f56d-436e-9309-aa9c7ce3989f","uuid":"e584420c-9644-4586-9160-d571c72b0a05","request_id":"req_011Cd4UFvGF9mqTz4Be7QdWA","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"K1EV format research (read-only)"}
