{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cd4UH1PM77eQ2SfNbAND2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Enough context gathered. Here is the test plan.\n\n## Test Plan: K1EV Buffered Capture Parser (host-side)\n\n**File naming (repo convention observed):** `tests/test_k1ev_capture_replay.py` — matches `test_<module>_<scenario>.py`; \"replay\" since it's parsing a captured serial dump, consistent with `test_paired_novelty_source_replay.py` / `test_novelty_decimation_smoothing.py`. Style observed: load the parser module via `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location` (module lives in `scripts/regression-harness/`), plain `assert`, module-defined exception class (e.g. `K1EVCaptureParseError`) raised and matched via string content in `str(exc)`, no pytest fixtures needed for pure-function parsing — matches `test_k1_real_music_corpus_capture.py` style exactly.\n\nNote: the actual host-side parser module doesn't appear to exist yet (only `capture/parse_capture.py` referenced in comments, and it's for the NOV/CAD format, not K1EV) — implementer needs to either locate/extend that parser for K1EV lines or write a new small one; test plan below assumes a `parse_k1ev_capture(lines: list[str]) -> K1EVCaptureRun` style function.\n\n### 1. Wrapper line parsing\n- `test_parses_begin_line_fields` — `K1EV_CAPTURE_BEGIN,count=1234,capacity=65536,dropped=0` extracts count/capacity/dropped as ints.\n- `test_parses_done_line_fields` — `K1EV_CAPTURE_DONE,count=1234,dropped=0` extracts count/dropped.\n- `test_begin_capacity_matches_compiled_constant` — assert parsed `capacity == 65536` (the `K1EV_CAPTURE_CAPACITY` value from `k1ev_capture.h`); this is a repo-truth pin, not just a parse check — if firmware ever resizes the ring this test should be the tripwire.\n- `test_begin_done_count_and_dropped_agree` — BEGIN.count == DONE.count and BEGIN.dropped == DONE.dropped (dump doesn't mutate these between begin/end, so a mismatch means truncated/garbled capture).\n- `test_dropped_nonzero_implies_count_hit_capacity` — semantic invariant: if `dropped > 0` then `count == capacity` (per `k1ev_capture_tick`, drops only happen once `count >= capacity`); a capture with drops but count < capacity is invalid evidence.\n\n### 2. Base-only sample line (no `has_chroma`, i.e. onset-only frame not landing on the decimation stride)\n- `test_parses_base_line_field_types` — `t_ms`, `event_ms`, `ev`, `kid`, `sid`, `hid` parse as ints (unsigned, so reject negative); `bphase`, `bconf` parse as float with exactly 3 decimal places; `bpm` as float with exactly 1 decimal place; `onset/bass/kick/snare/hihat/beat` parse as `0`/`1` ints (bool-coercible), never `True`/`False` strings.\n- `test_base_line_omits_chroma_fields` — assert `croot`, `ctype`, `cconf`, `chroma`, `mode`, `photons` are all absent/None on a base-only line (regex or key-existence check) — this is the has_chroma=0 branch and worth its own test since it's easy for a naive parser to assume every field is always present and silently default garbage.\n\n### 3. `has_chroma` sample line\n- `test_parses_chroma_line_full_fields` — same base fields plus `croot` (int, range -1..11), `ctype` (int enum 0..4), `cconf` (float, 3dp), `chroma` (exactly 12 semicolon-separated floats, each 3dp), `mode` (uint), `photons` (float, no fixed decimal count — full precision, per source comment \"photons stored full-precision because director scalar has no bounded range\").\n- `test_chroma_list_has_exactly_twelve_values` — explicit count assertion; guards against `K1_CHROMA_PC_BINS` drifting without the parser noticing (off-by-one would silently misalign chroma[11] into \"mode=\").\n\n### 4. croot/ctype sentinel invariant\n- `test_croot_negative_one_implies_ctype_none` — validator-level semantic check (not just parse): whenever `croot == -1`, `ctype` must equal `0` (NONE), per `k1ev_capture.cpp:139-140` (`have_chord ? rootNote : -1`). Conversely a non-`-1` croot should never pair with `ctype == 0`. This is the one place a firmware regression (e.g. forgetting to sync croot/ctype together) would silently produce nonsensical harmonic data downstream — worth asserting on every parsed sample line, not just as a unit test of one line.\n\n### 5. Malformed / truncated line handling\n- `test_truncated_chroma_line_raises` — a `has_chroma`-flagged-looking line cut off mid-`chroma=` list (e.g. only 8 of 12 values) should raise a clear parser error, not silently return a short list or wrong `mode`/`photons`. Match repo convention: raise a module-specific exception class with a message substring assertion (`\"chroma\"` or `\"truncated\"` in `str(exc)`), mirroring `RealCorpusCaptureError` pattern.\n- `test_unparseable_line_raises` — garbage line (e.g. partial write, binary noise, or a line missing the `[K1EV]` prefix entirely) raises rather than being silently skipped or coerced to zeros. Decide once: does the parser skip non-`[K1EV]` lines (e.g. blank lines, other serial chatter) intentionally, vs raise on a line that starts with `[K1EV]` but is truncated? Test should cover both cases distinctly — skip-non-matching vs raise-on-malformed-matching.\n- `test_missing_begin_or_done_marker_raises` — a lines list with sample lines but no `K1EV_CAPTURE_BEGIN`/`_DONE` wrapper should raise (can't validate count without it), not silently return whatever it parsed.\n\n### 6. Count/DONE consistency across parsed sample lines\n- `test_parsed_sample_count_matches_done_count` — number of successfully parsed `[K1EV]` sample lines equals `DONE.count` exactly (no drops-adjustment needed since dropped frames are never written to the buffer/dump in the first place — per `k1ev_capture_tick`, a dropped frame just increments the counter and returns before ever touching `K1EV_CAPTURE_BUFFER`). This is an equality invariant, not a \"minus expected drops\" one — worth stating explicitly in the test docstring since it's a common source of off-by-N assumptions.\n\n### 7. Additional edge cases from the real emit code\n- `test_flags_bit_decoding_matches_source_field_order` — cross-check that `onset/bass/kick/snare/hihat/beat` booleans in the *printed* line correspond to bits `0x01,0x02,0x04,0x08,0x10,0x20` per `k1ev_capture.cpp:128-134` — i.e. if the parser independently reconstructs flags from the printed 0/1 fields it should match a hand-built bitmask for a synthetic fixture line.\n- `test_event_id_fields_are_nonnegative_and_can_be_large` — `event_id`/`kick_event_id`/`snare_event_id`/`hihat_event_id` are `uint32_t`; fixture with a large value (e.g. `4294967295`) should parse without overflow/sign issues (Python ints are unbounded but worth asserting the parser doesn't apply a signed cast).\n- `test_bpm_always_one_decimal_place` — a fixture value like `bpm=120.0` (not `120` or `120.00`) — string-format regex check, since the field is a fixed `%.1f` and a permissive parser might accept `120` and silently miscompare downstream tooling expecting a decimal.\n- `test_bphase_bconf_cconf_chroma_always_three_decimal_places` — same discipline for the `%.3f` fields; catches a parser that's too permissive on format and would mask a firmware format-string regression.\n- `test_multiple_sample_lines_mixed_base_and_chroma_in_one_capture` — realistic fixture: BEGIN → several base-only lines interleaved with has_chroma lines (mirrors real onset-vs-decimation-stride emission) → DONE; parser must classify each line correctly and the aggregate count must still match DONE.count. This is the main \"does the whole pipeline hang together\" test, complementary to the narrower per-line tests above.\n\n**Not recommended (redundant):** don't duplicate a \"does capacity==65536\" check per-line — pin it once at the wrapper level. Don't write a separate test for every individual flag bit combination (2^6) — one fixture with a representative subset (e.g. onset+beat set, kick+hihat set, all-clear) is sufficient given the flags are independent bitwise ORs with no cross-field logic (unlike croot/ctype which do need the explicit invariant test in §4).\n\nI did not write any code or files — this is the design-only pass as requested. Now completing the Ruflo task."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":127372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":278,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019hSTdbYSrDRtayTkVr2QNF","session_id":"16a76e6c-f56d-436e-9309-aa9c7ce3989f","uuid":"0137ed8d-46f7-4262-bcd0-1fc6da45f745","request_id":"req_011Cd4UGzKbuDYHFc1RQtmVR","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"K1EV test design (read-only)"}
