{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cd4UMKFFTFQFJGQ7AhH1a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013N9Y1C3fbUG1Hgeccu4BBw","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"K1EV parser/validator implementation","subagent_type":"general-purpose","name":"k1ev-implementer","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are executing Ruflo task-1784147113063-miy978 (agent id k1ev-implementer) in a hierarchical Ruflo swarm (swarm-1784147099433-oai2dm) for the K1 firmware repo at /private/tmp/k1-ruflo-live.\n\nScope: implement a reusable host-side parser/validator for the buffered `[K1EV]` telemetry capture wire format, plus focused pytest tests. NO firmware edits (do not touch anything under SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/). This is a real reusable regression-harness module, not busywork — it must actually validate the frozen wire format so future device captures can be checked offline.\n\n## Verified format (from completed Ruflo research task, do not re-derive — trust this, it was verified against the actual snprintf/println call sites in k1ev_capture.cpp, not just header comments):\n\nWrapper lines (`USBSerial.println`, i.e. `\\r\\n`-terminated in the raw stream but treat line-splitting generically):\n- `K1EV_CAPTURE_BEGIN,count=<u32>,capacity=<u32>,dropped=<u32>`\n- `K1EV_CAPTURE_DONE,count=<u32>,dropped=<u32>` (no capacity field)\n\nPer-sample base line (always present, single line prefixed `[K1EV] `):\n```\n[K1EV] t_ms=%lu event_ms=%lu ev=%lu onset=%d bass=%d kick=%d snare=%d hihat=%d kid=%lu sid=%lu hid=%lu beat=%d bphase=%.3f bconf=%.3f bpm=%.1f\n```\n- t_ms, event_ms, ev (=event_id), kid (=kick_event_id), sid (=snare_event_id), hid (=hihat_event_id): unsigned ints (uint32 domain, parse as int, must be >=0).\n- onset/bass/kick/snare/hihat/beat: 0 or 1 (int flags). `beat` here is the tempo flywheel beat_tick, NOT ev.beat — no parser-visible difference, just document it in a docstring.\n- bphase, bconf: floats in the printed range [-32.768, 32.767] in practice near 0..1 (they're int16 q1000 re-expanded), always exactly 3 decimal digits as printed by `%.3f`.\n- bpm: float, always exactly 1 decimal digit (`%.1f`).\n\nOptional suffix, appended ONLY when the row is a decimated \"sample_frame\" (independent of onset/beat — detect its presence by the literal substring `\" croot=\"` in the line, do NOT infer from onset/beat flags since a row can be both onset AND sample_frame simultaneously):\n```\n croot=%d ctype=%d cconf=%.3f chroma=<v0>;<v1>;...;<v11> mode=%u photons=%.3f\n```\n- croot: int, range -1..11. -1 is the sentinel meaning chord type NONE (A-origin root pitch class otherwise).\n- ctype: int 0..4 enum: 0=NONE, 1=MAJOR, 2=MINOR, 3=DIMINISHED, 4=AUGMENTED.\n- cconf: float, 3 decimals (`%.3f`).\n- chroma: EXACTLY 12 semicolon-separated floats, each `%.3f` (3 decimals) — pitch-class bins, A-origin (bin 0 = A).\n- mode: unsigned int (`%u`), applied_mode.\n- photons: float, printed with `%.3f` (3 decimals; this is pinned in the actual format string, not default C printf precision).\n\nSemantic invariant to validate (not just parse): croot == -1 if and only if ctype == 0 (NONE). A row where these disagree is a data integrity bug and the validator must flag it.\n\nSample-line count must equal the `count=` field in the `K1EV_CAPTURE_DONE` line exactly (dropped frames never reach the buffer in the first place, so no adjustment for `dropped` is needed against the emitted line count — `dropped` just reports frames that hit capacity and were never appended).\n\n## Test plan (from completed Ruflo research task — implement ALL of these as real pytest tests, no fewer):\n\n1. Wrapper line parsing: BEGIN fields (count/capacity/dropped), DONE fields (count/dropped, no capacity) extracted correctly; capacity==65536 sanity-pinned in a fixture (this repo pins K1EV_CAPTURE_CAPACITY=65536 in firmware — the parser should not hardcode 65536 as a requirement, but a fixture/golden capture SHOULD use it and assert it round-trips).\n2. Base-only sample line (no `croot=` substring): correct field extraction and correct type coercion (ints vs floats); assert the parsed record has no chroma/chord/mode/photons populated (use `None` or absent, whichever fits the module's dataclass design).\n3. has_chroma sample line: correct extraction of croot, ctype, cconf, all 12 chroma floats (order preserved), mode, photons.\n4. croot==-1 <=> ctype==NONE semantic invariant: a validator function that raises/flags when this is violated, with both a positive (consistent) and negative (violated) test case.\n5. Malformed/truncated line handling: parser must raise a clear, module-defined exception (not silently return garbage or None) on a truncated/malformed `[K1EV]` line or corrupted wrapper line. Follow this repo's existing convention — look at how `tests/test_k1_real_music_corpus_capture.py` (or a similar existing capture test file in tests/) defines and raises its own exception class, and mirror that pattern for a `K1EVCaptureParseError` (or similarly named) exception.\n6. Exact count equality: number of successfully parsed `[K1EV]` sample lines equals the DONE line's `count=` field, for a well-formed synthetic capture fixture.\n7. Precision/bitmask edge cases: bpm always 1 decimal, bphase/bconf/cconf/chroma always 3 decimals (these are format guarantees baked into the firmware printf specs — test that the parser doesn't choke on values like `bpm=120.0` or `bconf=0.000` or negative-looking edge values), flags 0/1 ints for onset/bass/kick/snare/hihat/beat, a realistic mixed fixture with both base-only and has_chroma lines interleaved (mirroring the real decimation cadence — has_chroma every 3rd sample_frame row OR any explicit onset row, base-only otherwise).\n\n## Deliverables\n\n1. New module: `scripts/regression-harness/k1ev_capture_parse.py` (or `parse_k1ev_capture.py` — pick a name consistent with sibling files like `apstream_ingest.py`, `device_novelty_replay.py` in that directory; check existing naming pattern first via `ls scripts/regression-harness/`). Should expose something like a `K1EVCaptureRun` / `K1EVSample` dataclass, a `parse_k1ev_capture(text: str) -> K1EVCaptureRun` (or similar) function, and a validator function for the croot/ctype invariant. Keep it a plain, reusable, no-heap-analogy-needed Python module — no CLI framework needed unless the sibling files in that dir universally use one (check first; match house style, don't invent new conventions).\n2. New test file: `tests/test_k1ev_capture_replay.py` (the name recommended by the test-design research; matches `test_<module>_<scenario>.py` convention) implementing all 7 test categories above as real pytest test functions with clear names and docstrings. Use synthetic fixture strings built inline (following the style of `test_k1_real_music_corpus_capture.py` if it has similar synthetic-capture-text fixtures) — do NOT require real device hardware or real capture files.\n3. Do not touch anything under SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/, platformio.ini, or any file outside scripts/regression-harness/ and tests/.\n\n## Verification (you must do this yourself before finishing)\n\n- Run `pytest tests/test_k1ev_capture_replay.py -v` and confirm ALL new tests pass. Fix any failures yourself.\n- Run `git diff --check` to confirm no whitespace-error violations in your new files.\n- Run `git status` to confirm only your two new files (plus maybe an `__init__.py` if genuinely needed) are untracked/changed — nothing under SPECTRASYNQ_K1_FIRMWARE/ should show as modified.\n- Do NOT run the full `pytest tests/` suite unless you want extra confidence (fine to do it, but the gate that matters here is scoped: your new test file must be green and must not have broken anything by import side-effects).\n\n## Reporting\n\nWhen finished, report back (as your final message, this is what gets returned) with:\n- Exact file paths created\n- Full `pytest tests/test_k1ev_capture_replay.py -v` output (or a clear summary: N passed, 0 failed)\n- `git status --short` output\n- Whether `git diff --check` was clean\n- Any blockers encountered and how you resolved them, or state clearly if something couldn't be resolved and needs a decision\n\nThen call mcp__ruflo__task_complete with taskId \"task-1784147113063-miy978\" and a result object summarizing files created + test pass count. Then call mcp__ruflo__hooks_task-completed with taskId \"task-1784147113063-miy978\", success true (or false if you could not get tests green — in that case explain why in the result).\n\nDo NOT commit anything yourself — leave the git state as-is for the orchestrator to review, gate, and commit."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1900,"cache_read_input_tokens":189162,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1900},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16a76e6c-f56d-436e-9309-aa9c7ce3989f","uuid":"e944be0b-3a70-4678-8273-a8285c6abd35","request_id":"req_011Cd4UMHvNsuX2R3iEVgG8d"}
